    "title": "pandas.Timestamp.day — pandas 3.1.0.dev0 documentation",
    "status": 200,
    "markdown": "# pandas.Timestamp.day#\n\n- Timestamp.day#\n- Return the day of the Timestamp. Days are numbered from 1 through the number of days in the month. \n  - Returns:\n    - int\n    - The day of the Timestamp.\n See also \n  - `Timestamp.week`\n  - Return the week number of the year.\n  - `Timestamp.weekday`\n  - Return the day of the week.\n Examples >>> ts = pd.Timestamp(\"2024-08-31 16:16:30\") >>> ts.day 31",
